# Rust
target/
# isolated per-cudf-root target dirs for cudf (default-feature) builds — see
# scripts/build-test*.sh (target-cudf-<cudf_root_basename>, e.g. target-cudf-rapids,
# target-cudf-rapids-cuda-12.2). Glob covers the plain legacy target-cudf too.
target-cudf*/

# CMake / C++ build artifacts
cpp/build/
cpp/install/

# Editor / IDE
compile_commands.json
.cache
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Generated FlatBuffers code (built from flatbuffers/gpu_plan.fbs)
cpp/include/generated/
peacockdb-core/src/generated/

# OS
.DS_Store
cufile.log

# DuckDB cost-oracle cache (generated, not committed)
testdata/*/.duckdb_cache/

# Python bytecode (duckdb_cost.py tests)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local-only embedding source cache (fetch_embeddings.sh); never committed — data ships as parquet
testdata/embeddings-cache/

# Agent working directory: this repo is developed by the ensemble in llm-wiki/prompts.md,
# and .claude/ is per-checkout tooling config, not project state.
.claude/

# The 26.02 build tree; cpp/build (25.02) is covered above and this one was not,
# so a `git add cpp` swept 1069 build artifacts into a commit once.
cpp/build26/

# (was: testdata/benchmark-results/tpch.sf40/ — ignored while the sf40 case list was
# still moving and every collection would have committed files about to be renamed away.
# Both halves of that reason are gone: sf40 is now the ONLY tier timed — sf1 measures
# mostly the host prologue and is not benchmarked at all — and the tree is one file per
# (dataset, mode) rather than one per query, so a collection rewrites two files instead
# of thirty-two. The measurement is the deliverable, and it is committed.)
